## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/ohlc/{candle_size}

OHLC

Returns the Open High Low Close (OHLC) candle data for a given ticker.

Results are limited to 2,500 elements even if there are more available.

Row order depends on `candle_size`: intraday candles are newest first, while daily candles are oldest
first. The most recent intraday candle is still forming, and its `start_time` is the start of the current
bucket. Select the latest bar by the maximum `start_time`, not by array position.

Note: If you select 1d or 1w as a candle_size then the candles won't have a start & end time. For 1w, the `date` field is the Monday of the ISO week.

Note: Suppose you enter end_date value 2024-11-25 which was a Monday. Your response will include 1-2 hours of data from Tuesday 2024-11-26 due to UTC date rollover.
Rest-assured, the response data covers the full trading day (based on Eastern time) according to your entered end_date.


### Fully resolved operation
```json
{
  "key": "GET /api/stock/{ticker}/ohlc/{candle_size}",
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/api/stock/{ticker}/ohlc/{candle_size}",
  "transport": "http-rest",
  "operation": {
    "callbacks": {},
    "description": "Returns the Open High Low Close (OHLC) candle data for a given ticker.\n\nResults are limited to 2,500 elements even if there are more available.\n\nRow order depends on `candle_size`: intraday candles are newest first, while daily candles are oldest\nfirst. The most recent intraday candle is still forming, and its `start_time` is the start of the current\nbucket. Select the latest bar by the maximum `start_time`, not by array position.\n\nNote: If you select 1d or 1w as a candle_size then the candles won't have a start & end time. For 1w, the `date` field is the Monday of the ISO week.\n\nNote: Suppose you enter end_date value 2024-11-25 which was a Monday. Your response will include 1-2 hours of data from Tuesday 2024-11-26 due to UTC date rollover.\nRest-assured, the response data covers the full trading day (based on Eastern time) according to your entered end_date.\n",
